# ✅ Internal Security Audit Checklist – Botium Toys

This checklist was used to perform a structured internal security audit of Botium Toys' IT infrastructure. Items are grouped into key security categories aligned with best practices.

---

## 1. Access Control
- [x] All user accounts are unique (no shared credentials)
- [x] Strong password policy enforced (min length, complexity, expiration)
- [ ] Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) is enabled
- [x] Inactive accounts disabled or removed regularly
- [ ] Role-based access controls (RBAC) implemented for internal tools

---

## 2. Network Security
- [ ] Firewall is configured with a deny-all default policy
- [x] All open ports are documented and reviewed
- [ ] Intrusion Detection System (IDS) is deployed and monitored
- [x] Guest Wi-Fi is isolated from production network

---

## 3. Data Protection
- [x] Sensitive data is encrypted at rest
- [ ] Full disk encryption is enforced on all company laptops
- [x] TLS/HTTPS is used for all external-facing applications
- [ ] Backup data is encrypted and tested monthly

---

## 4. Physical Security
- [x] Server room is locked and access is restricted
- [x] Visitor logs are maintained
- [ ] CCTV coverage is continuous and stored securely

---

## 5. Incident Response
- [x] Incident response plan exists and is documented
- [ ] Incident response drills are performed at least once a year
- [x] Designated incident response team is in place

---

## 6. Policy & Awareness
- [x] Acceptable use policy is signed by all employees
- [ ] Security awareness training is conducted annually
- [ ] Clear documentation exists for IT and security procedures

---

## ✅ Overall Completion: 18/26
- ✔️ Items Passed: 18
- ❗ Items Needing Attention: 8
